.guide-zone th{background:#f4f4f5}
</style><div class="guide-zone"><p>SOPHIA · TIKTOK SLIDESHOW PROGRAMME</p><p><strong>Creator Guide</strong></p><p>Your onboarding — read this first</p><p>Welcome to the team. This is your onboarding document — everything you need, in one place. It covers what the job is, how you get paid, how to set up and warm up your TikTok account, how to publish a slideshow, and what decides whether you continue after the trial week. Your hiring manager sent you this along with your login; there is nothing else to read.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Read this fully before your first post.</strong></p><p>Almost every problem we see — no views, a paused contract, a rejected post — comes from skipping something in here. Fifteen minutes now saves you a lot of trouble.</p></th></tr></thead></table><h2><strong>Your login</strong></h2><p>Your hiring manager fills these in for you. Keep them somewhere safe.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Platform</strong></p></th><th><p>https://sophia-marketing-orga.vercel.app</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Your email</strong></p></th><th><p>First name + first letter of your last name @sophia.com</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Your password</strong></p></th><th><p>12345678</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Your hiring manager</strong></p></th><th><p>The person who sent you this document — reach them on Upwork or Slack</p></th></tr></thead></table><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Your first day, in four moves:</strong></p><p>1. Log in to the platform and read this guide.  2. Create your TikTok account with the exact handle shown in your space.  3. Press “Start warm-up” and leave it 24 hours.  4. Your slideshows appear the next day — then you post twice a day, every day.</p></th></tr></thead></table><h1><strong>1. Your checklist</strong></h1><p>The whole job on one page. Everything is explained in detail further down.</p><h2><strong>Before your first post</strong></h2><ul><li>Log in to the Sophia platform with the details your manager sent you.</li><li>Read this guide.</li><li>Create your TikTok account with the exact handle shown in your space.</li><li>Use your own email address for it — an existing one or a new one you create.</li><li>Press “Start warm-up” on the platform.</li><li>Use TikTok normally for 24 hours — scroll, like, follow, comment.</li><li>Wait for your slideshows to appear in your calendar the next day.</li><li>Join Slack.</li></ul><h2><strong>Every single day</strong></h2><ul><li>Open the platform and find today's slideshows in your calendar.</li><li>Download the images.</li><li>Build post 1 on TikTok — correct order, caption provided, sound provided.</li><li>Publish it and paste the link back on the platform.</li><li>Do the same for post 2, later in the day.</li><li>Check the comments on your recent posts and reply.</li><li>Check for any review your manager sent you and fix it on the next post.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>2 posts per day, 7 days a week — including during your trial week.</strong></p><p>There is no 1-post-per-day period. It is two from your very first posting day.</p></th></tr></thead></table><h1><strong>2. What you are doing</strong></h1><p>You are helping to promote Sophia, a general knowledge app. We promote it by posting slideshows on TikTok — images with text on them.</p><p>Here is an example: <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/@studyavec_lea/photo/7660178099220352289">view the post on TikTok</a></p><p>All images, captions and sounds are prepared for you. Your job is to assemble them into a TikTok slideshow, publish it, and paste the link back on the platform — twice a day, every day.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>The task itself is simple. The value you bring is consistency: posting every single day, at good times, with tidy formatting.</strong></p></th></tr></thead></table><h2><strong>Your terms</strong></h2><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Trial week</strong></p></th><th><p>$7 fixed — set up your account, warm it up, then post</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>After the trial</strong></p></th><th><p>$27 per month fixed</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Posting volume</strong></p></th><th><p>2 posts per day, 7 days a week — from your first posting day</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Sound</strong></p></th><th><p>You use the sound provided with each slideshow on the system</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Post links</strong></p></th><th><p>Pasted back on the platform after each post</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Contract type</strong></p></th><th><p>Fixed price, through Upwork</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Language</strong></p></th><th><p>You publish only in your own language</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Location</strong></p></th><th><p>You must be physically present in your country</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Growing</strong></p></th><th><p>Strong creators can manage more than one account — up to $27/month each</p></th></tr></thead></table><h2><strong>Continuing after the trial week</strong></h2><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>The trial week decides whether you continue. It is not automatic.</strong></p><p>We continue with creators who post good-quality slideshows, post consistently twice a day at sensible times, and whose account is actually getting views. If the quality is sloppy, the posting is irregular, or the account gets no traction, the contract ends at the end of the trial week.</p></th></tr></thead></table><p>So treat the trial week as the real thing, because it is. The three things we look at:</p><ol><li>Quality — slides well formatted, correct sound, correct every day.</li><li>Consistency — 2 posts a day, every day, at stable times.</li><li>Views — the account is getting traction, not flat or shadow-banned.</li></ol><h1><strong>3. Getting set up</strong></h1><h2><strong>Step 1 — Log in to the platform</strong></h2><p>Go to <a href="https://sophia-marketing-orga.vercel.app/">sophia-marketing-orga.vercel.app</a> and sign in with the details your manager sent you:</p><table><thead><tr><th><p>