ced tidily and fully inside the frame</li><li>Text large enough to read on a phone, but not overwhelming the image</li><li>Images in the intended order</li><li>The sound provided on the system</li><li>Correct format and aspect ratio</li><li>Captions exactly as provided</li><li>Publishing only in your own language</li><li>The post link pasted back on the platform</li></ul></th><th><ul><li>Text so large it covers the image</li><li>Text cut off at the edges or hidden behind the TikTok UI</li><li>A sound you picked yourself</li><li>Images out of order or missing</li><li>Low-quality, stretched or squashed images</li><li>Publishing in a language that isn't yours</li><li>Leaving comments unanswered</li><li>Forgetting to paste the link</li></ul></th></tr></thead></table><h2><strong>Comments</strong></h2><p>Check the comments on your posts. Reply where it makes sense, and don't leave questions hanging — engagement helps the post, and an abandoned comment section looks like an abandoned account.</p><h1><strong>5. Reviews &amp; feedback</strong></h1><p>Your manager checks your posts regularly and can send you feedback directly through the platform as a pop-up review. This is normal and not a warning — it is how we keep quality consistent across every country.</p><p>Common feedback you might get:</p><ul><li>Text too large, or badly placed</li><li>Wrong sound, or no sound</li><li>Wrong format</li><li>Low image quality</li><li>Irregular posting times, or a missed post</li><li>Comments left unattended</li><li>Link not pasted on the platform</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>When you get a review, apply the correction on your next post — not eventually.</strong></p><p>The same feedback given three times becomes a problem for your contract. Fixed the first time, it is simply a note.</p></th></tr></thead></table><h2><strong>What your manager checks every day</strong></h2><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Did you post twice?</strong></p></th><th><p>2 posts per day, every day</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Are the links on the platform?</strong></p></th><th><p>One link pasted per published post</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Are you getting views?</strong></p></th><th><p>Zero views usually means the account wasn't warmed up properly</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Are the posts correct?</strong></p></th><th><p>Text placement, provided sound, format, image quality</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Are your times consistent?</strong></p></th><th><p>Peak hours, roughly the same slots each day</p></th></tr></thead></table><h1><strong>6. Getting paid</strong></h1><p>Everything runs through Upwork — your contract, your milestones, and your payments. There are no side payments, and you should never be asked for one.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Trial week</strong></p></th><th><p>$7, released once the trial week is complete</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Monthly</strong></p></th><th><p>$27 per month, as a fixed-price milestone</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Requirement</strong></p></th><th><p>2 posts per day, 7 days a week</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Where</strong></p></th><th><p>Upwork only</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>Questions</strong></p></th><th><p>Message your hiring manager on Upwork or Slack</p></th></tr></thead></table><h2><strong>Missed posts</strong></h2><p>Missing the odd post happens, and we handle it with a conversation rather than money. But posting is the job, so there is a clear rule when it becomes a pattern:</p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Up to 5 missed posts in a month</strong></p></th><th><p>No deduction — your manager will talk to you about it</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>More than 5 missed in a month</strong></p></th><th><p>$1 is deducted per missed post</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>How it is applied</strong></p></th><th><p>Taken off that month's payment, or from the next month if that payment has already gone out</p></th></tr></thead></table><p>If something genuinely comes up — illness, an emergency — tell your manager straight away rather than going quiet. A message costs you nothing; silence is what ends contracts. If you are unresponsive for 4 days, the contract is ended and we request a refund.</p><h1><strong>7. Slack &amp; questions</strong></h1><p>We have a Slack workspace for the whole programme. Join it as soon as you are hired — it is where you ask questions and follow updates.</p><p><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/sophia-system/shared_invite/zt-44pqj3z39-X4KkPQI6cwOwWE2LNaLbig">Join the Sophia Slack</a></p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>#welcome</strong></p></th><th><p>Start here — pinned onboarding information</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>#questions</strong></p></th><th><p>Ask anything — your manager or another manager will answer</p></th></tr><tr><th><p><strong>#technical-issues</strong></p></th><th><p>Platform bugs, login problems, TikTok account problems</p></th></tr></thead></table><p><strong>Remember: your daily post links do not go in Slack. They go on the platform.</strong></p><p><em>Please ask in the channels rather than by direct message. Your question has probably been asked before, and the answer helps everyone else too.</em></p><h2><strong>Quick answers</strong></h2><h3><strong>I created my TikTok account but my manager can't find it.</strong></h3><p>Send them the direct link to your profile. If you didn't use exactly the handle shown in your Sophia space, either correct it or ask your manager to update it in the system.</p><h3><strong>Which email should I use for the TikTok account?</strong></h3><p>Your own — an existing address, or a new one you create for this. It is your account.</p><h3><strong>Can I use a different sound if I think it fits better?</strong></h3><p>No. Use the sound provided with the slideshow on the system.</p><h3><strong>I posted in the wrong language by mistake.</strong></h3><p>If it's getting good views, leave it. From then on, publish only in your own language.</p><h3><strong>My posts are getting no views at all.</strong></h3><p>Almost always an account that wasn't warmed up for a full 24 hours, or that started posting too early. Tell your manager — don't just keep posting into the void.</p><h3><strong>No slideshows have appeared in my calendar.</strong></h3><p>Check that your 24-hour warm-up has finished. If it has and there is still nothing, message your manager or post in #technical-issues. Don't invent your own content.</p><h3><strong>I can't post today.</strong></h3><p>Tell your manager before the deadline, not after. Planned absences are manageable; unexplained silence isn't.</p><h2><strong>The rules, short version</strong></h2><ul><li>Press “Start warm-up” and wait a full 24 hours before your first post.</li><li>2 posts per day, 7 days a week — including your trial week.</li><li>Use the sound provided on the system.</li><li>Paste every post link back on the platform.</li><li>Use exactly the TikTok identity assigned to you, with your own email address.</li><li>Only publish in your own language.</li><li>Apply feedback on your next post.</li><li>Everything goes through Upwork.</li><li>If something goes wrong, message your manager the same day.</li></ul></div>$guide_zone_c$ as html
)
insert into public.documents (cle, titre, titre_en, audience, ordre, contenu, contenu_en)
select 'guide_poster_zone_c', 'Creator Guide — Zone C (lower rate)', 'Creator Guide — Zone C (lower rate)', 'poster', 5, html, html
from src
on conflict (cle) do update set
  titre = excluded.titre,
  titre_en = excluded.titre_en,
  audience = excluded.audience,
  ordre = excluded.ordre,
  contenu = excluded.contenu,
  contenu_en = excluded.contenu_en,
  updated_at = now();
